            <title>[PARQUET-212] Implement nested type read rules in parquet-thrift</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-212</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Need to implement the rules from &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-113&quot; title=&quot;Clarify parquet-format specification for LIST and MAP structures.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;PARQUET-113&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;PARQUET-113&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in parquet-thrift. Similar to &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-193&quot; title=&quot;Avro: Implement read compatibility rules for nested types&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;PARQUET-193&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;PARQUET-193&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, which tracked the read-side updates to parquet-avro.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
